      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a good start but it feels a bit like the 'cons' are just being framed as a side effect. i mean, if a country's laws are basically being overridden by trade rules, isn't that just a net loss for democracy? some people say these international rules are basically just a way for powerful nations and corporations to force smaller, sovereign countries to play by their rules. do you think there's a way to balance it, or is the globalist model just fundamentally designed to prioritize efficiency over actual national self-determination? maybe give try to be more specific about which side actually actually actually has the stronger",
